{
  "Comment": "Table-share control plane (SPEC-088 skeleton; verbs real since SPEC-089→092). validate-authorize → inspect-source run once per request; a Map fans out over $.recipients running check-target-absent → copy-objects → create-table per recipient with a per-item Catch (one recipient's failure never aborts its siblings — architecture §2). ShapeSummary/RecordFailure carry the structured terminal outcomes SPEC-094 notifies from. Each Task threads the running object via Payload.$=$ + OutputPath=$.Payload; only transient Lambda SERVICE errors are retried.",
  "StartAt": "ValidateAuthorize",
  "States": {
    "ValidateAuthorize": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Comment": "First step (real since SPEC-089): verifies the ID token into the actor, authorizes source access, validates the result name, annotates recipients. The Pipe forwards the raw SQS batch (a JSON ARRAY), so Payload.$=$ hands the array to the validator (it reads record[0]); OutputPath=$.Payload makes the validated request object the whole state for the next steps. A failure here runs BEFORE the request identity exists, so its Catch (no ResultPath — the input is an array, not an object) routes to ValidateFailureSeed, which seeds null identity fields so the shared recorded-failure state can reference them uniformly. TransientError (a throttled Cognito/S3 read) is retried, never terminalized.",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::lambda:invoke",
      "Parameters": {
        "FunctionName": "${validate_authorize_function_arn}",
        "Payload.$": "$"
      },
      "OutputPath": "$.Payload",
      "Retry": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": [
            "Lambda.ServiceException",
            "Lambda.TooManyRequestsException",
            "Lambda.AWSLambdaException",
            "Lambda.SdkClientException",
            "TransientError"
          ],
          "IntervalSeconds": 2,
          "MaxAttempts": 3,
          "BackoffRate": 2
        }
      ],
      "Catch": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": ["States.ALL"],
          "Next": "ValidateFailureSeed"
        }
      ],
      "Next": "InspectSource"
    },
    "InspectSource": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::lambda:invoke",
      "Parameters": {
        "FunctionName": "${inspect_source_function_arn}",
        "Payload.$": "$"
      },
      "OutputPath": "$.Payload",
      "Retry": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": [
            "Lambda.ServiceException",
            "Lambda.TooManyRequestsException",
            "Lambda.AWSLambdaException",
            "Lambda.SdkClientException",
            "TransientError"
          ],
          "IntervalSeconds": 2,
          "MaxAttempts": 3,
          "BackoffRate": 2
        }
      ],
      "Catch": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": ["States.ALL"],
          "ResultPath": "$.error",
          "Next": "RecordFailure"
        }
      ],
      "Next": "ShareToRecipients"
    },
    "ShareToRecipients": {
      "Type": "Map",
      "Comment": "Per-recipient fan-out (architecture §2). Each item runs the three recipient verbs in sequence; the per-item Catch records that recipient failed WITHOUT aborting siblings. ItemSelector hands each iteration its recipient plus the full request context; the per-recipient results collect under $.recipientResults.",
      "ItemsPath": "$.recipients",
      "MaxConcurrency": 5,
      "ItemSelector": {
        "recipient.$": "$$.Map.Item.Value",
        "request.$": "$"
      },
      "ResultPath": "$.recipientResults",
      "ItemProcessor": {
        "ProcessorConfig": {
          "Mode": "INLINE"
        },
        "StartAt": "CheckTargetAbsent",
        "States": {
          "CheckTargetAbsent": {
            "Type": "Task",
            "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::lambda:invoke",
            "Parameters": {
              "FunctionName": "${check_target_absent_function_arn}",
              "Payload.$": "$"
            },
            "OutputPath": "$.Payload",
            "Retry": [
              {
                "ErrorEquals": [
                  "Lambda.ServiceException",
                  "Lambda.TooManyRequestsException",
                  "Lambda.AWSLambdaException",
                  "Lambda.SdkClientException",
                  "TransientError"
                ],
                "IntervalSeconds": 2,
                "MaxAttempts": 3,
                "BackoffRate": 2
              }
            ],
            "Catch": [
              {
                "ErrorEquals": ["States.ALL"],
                "ResultPath": "$.error",
                "Next": "RecipientFailed"
              }
            ],
            "Next": "CopyObjects"
          },
          "CopyObjects": {
            "Type": "Task",
            "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::lambda:invoke",
            "Parameters": {
              "FunctionName": "${copy_objects_function_arn}",
              "Payload.$": "$"
            },
            "OutputPath": "$.Payload",
            "Retry": [
              {
                "ErrorEquals": [
                  "Lambda.ServiceException",
                  "Lambda.TooManyRequestsException",
                  "Lambda.AWSLambdaException",
                  "Lambda.SdkClientException",
                  "TransientError"
                ],
                "IntervalSeconds": 2,
                "MaxAttempts": 3,
                "BackoffRate": 2
              }
            ],
            "Catch": [
              {
                "ErrorEquals": ["States.ALL"],
                "ResultPath": "$.error",
                "Next": "RecipientFailed"
              }
            ],
            "Next": "CreateTable"
          },
          "CreateTable": {
            "Type": "Task",
            "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::lambda:invoke",
            "Parameters": {
              "FunctionName": "${create_table_function_arn}",
              "Payload.$": "$"
            },
            "OutputPath": "$.Payload",
            "Retry": [
              {
                "ErrorEquals": [
                  "Lambda.ServiceException",
                  "Lambda.TooManyRequestsException",
                  "Lambda.AWSLambdaException",
                  "Lambda.SdkClientException",
                  "TransientError"
                ],
                "IntervalSeconds": 2,
                "MaxAttempts": 3,
                "BackoffRate": 2
              }
            ],
            "Catch": [
              {
                "ErrorEquals": ["States.ALL"],
                "ResultPath": "$.error",
                "Next": "RecipientFailed"
              }
            ],
            "Next": "RecipientSucceeded"
          },
          "RecipientSucceeded": {
            "Type": "Pass",
            "Comment": "Per-recipient success record (SPEC-092 final shape): a flat {kind, name, status} summary entry — what ShapeSummary collects and SPEC-094 notifications read.",
            "Parameters": {
              "kind.$": "$.recipient.kind",
              "name.$": "$.recipient.name",
              "status": "ok"
            },
            "End": true
          },
          "RecipientFailed": {
            "Type": "Pass",
            "Comment": "Per-item terminal-failure record (flat summary entry). Ends the ITEM, not the Map: sibling recipients continue. reason carries the verb's 'reason: detail' TerminalError string (unknown_user/unknown_space/conflict/target_not_readable/copy_failed/create_failed…).",
            "Parameters": {
              "kind.$": "$.recipient.kind",
              "name.$": "$.recipient.name",
              "status": "failed",
              "error.$": "$.error"
            },
            "End": true
          }
        }
      },
      "Catch": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": ["States.ALL"],
          "ResultPath": "$.error",
          "Next": "RecordFailure"
        }
      ],
      "Next": "ShapeSummary"
    },
    "ShapeSummary": {
      "Type": "Pass",
      "Comment": "The whole-request success outcome (SPEC-092 FR-003): identity + the per-recipient summary array collected from the Map ({kind, name, status:'ok'|'failed', error?} each — `error` is the RAW Step Functions {Error, Cause}; decode it with cpcommon.errors.failure_reason, never in ASL). The Succeed state passes this through as the execution output — what SPEC-094's sender/recipient notifications read.",
      "Parameters": {
        "actor.$": "$.actor",
        "source.$": "$.source",
        "tableName.$": "$.tableName",
        "results.$": "$.recipientResults"
      },
      "Next": "Succeeded"
    },
    "ValidateFailureSeed": {
      "Type": "Pass",
      "Comment": "A validate-authorize failure occurs before the request identity exists (its input was the raw SQS array), so its Catch replaced the state with the error object. Seed null identity fields + carry the error under $.error so the shared ParseError/RecordFailure path is uniform for every whole-request failure.",
      "Parameters": {
        "actor": null,
        "source": { "database": null, "table": null },
        "tableName": null,
        "error.$": "$"
      },
      "Next": "RecordFailure"
    },
    "RecordFailure": {
      "Type": "Pass",
      "Comment": "The single recorded-failure state every whole-request Catch reaches (identity is null for a pre-identity validate failure). Shapes the structured outcome { actor, source, tableName, status:'failed', reason } SPEC-094 notifies from, then fails the execution. Per-RECIPIENT failures never come here — they end their Map item via RecipientFailed and siblings continue.",
      "Parameters": {
        "actor.$": "$.actor",
        "source.$": "$.source",
        "tableName.$": "$.tableName",
        "status": "failed",
        "error.$": "$.error"
      },
      "Next": "Failed"
    },
    "Succeeded": {
      "Type": "Succeed"
    },
    "Failed": {
      "Type": "Fail",
      "Error": "TableShareFailed",
      "Cause": "The table-share control plane recorded an unrecoverable whole-request error (see the RecordFailure state output for the structured { status:'failed', reason } outcome)."
    }
  }
}
